# Testing and validation

Evidence before completion claims. Choose the **smallest verification that proves the changed behavior**, then expand when risk requires it.

## FAST

For localized UI/styling/copy changes: type/lint or targeted test as applicable; browser-check the affected workflow when behavior/layout matters. Do not run the entire Playwright or repository suite for a one-file cosmetic change unless required by the project or failure evidence.

## CONTROLLED

Run affected unit/integration tests plus the affected browser workflow where practical. Verify permissions, loading/empty/error states, and downstream behavior relevant to the change.

## HEAVY

Run the full relevant test/build/Playwright scope, cross-module checks, and explicit regression validation. Use the existing Superpowers verification/review skills when invoked by the task router.

## UI verification

For UI changes verify the real route/workflow, not only a screenshot. Check keyboard/focus, dialogs/drawers, loading, empty, errors, validation, responsive behavior, and permission visibility as applicable. Use safe UAT/seed data. Never expose PHI/PII.

## Figma

When a Figma URL exists, use `.cursor/rules/figma-mcp.mdc`, map designs to existing portal components/tokens, run the affected app workflow, and compare visually. Do not create a second design system.

## Cross-module

If shared UI, patient context, billing/payment, or SignalR helpers change, search consumers and expand validation to affected modules. Keep `ip-overlays-consolidated.test.ts` green for IP overlay work.
